==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[inter-operability]]

===Etymology===
{{suffix|interoperable|ity|lang=en}}; alternatively analyzed as {{prefix|inter|operability|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌɪntəɹɒpəɹəˈbɪləti/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|interoperabilities}}

# Interoperability is a property of a [[product]] or [[system]], whose [[interfaces]] are completely understood, to work with other products or systems, present or future, without any [[restricted]] access or [[implementation]].
# {{context|military|lang=en}} The [[capacity]] for a service, piece of equipment etc., to be operated by different forces or groups.
#* '''2010''', "Entente or bust", ''The Economist'', 14 Oct 2010:
#*: Dr Fox and Mr Morin have ruled out the notion of binational crews, but they are still exploring other ways to enhance the '''interoperability''' of France’s ''Charles de Gaulle'' and Britain’s planned two new carriers, which seem likely to be spared by the defence review.

